    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully fixed the bug and verified it works. Here's what I did:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`), even though the flag was being passed. When running `frai-gate init --ci` directly, it worked correctly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `frai` CLI's `gate` command was not properly passing the `--ci` flag to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI. The flag was being parsed at the Commander.js level but not included in the arguments passed to the spawned frai-gate process.\n\n## Solution\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-760) to:\n1. Accept the additional `options` and `command` parameters in the action callback\n2. Check if `--ci` is present in `process.argv`\n3. Add `--ci` to the arguments passed to the frai-gate CLI if it's found\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 **Test 1**: `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\n\u2705 **Test 2**: `frai gate init` (without `--ci`) still works correctly and only creates:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - No workflow directory\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `npx tsc` and the fix is ready to use. The changes are in the source file at `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` lines 753-756, where the `--ci` flag is now detected and passed through to frai-gate.",
